   74: /// The candidates are evaluated from the newest backwards, because the cost of dropping an
   75: /// early reasoning item is not its own size: dropping it also drops every reasoning item after
   76: /// it for free, and it is only worth paying for if the *later* reasoning is not going to force
   77: /// a break anyway. An earliest-first pass that stopped at the first profitable candidate would
   78: /// break the prefix too early and pay for a re-prefill that a later break would have covered.
   79: ///
   80: /// Reasoning belonging to `active_turn_id` is left undecided: the model is still following it,
   81: /// and its final size is not known yet.
   82: pub(crate) fn freeze_reasoning_retention(
